### 11. External Tables vs Managed Tables

| Aspect | Managed Table | External Table |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Data location** | Controlled by Unity Catalog (cloud storage managed by Databricks) | You control the storage path (`LOCATION 'abfss://...'`) |
| **DROP TABLE** | Deletes data + metadata | Deletes metadata only — data files remain |
| **Auto Optimize** | Full support | Full support |
| **Performance** | Slightly better (optimized storage layout) | Same for reads if well-organized |
| **Governance** | Full UC lineage + access control | Full UC lineage + access control |
| **Portability** | Tied to Databricks workspace | Data accessible outside Databricks |
| **Best for** | All internal analytics tables | Shared data lakes, multi-tool access, regulatory data retention |

> **Recommendation**: Use **managed tables** unless you have a specific reason to control the storage location (multi-cloud, external tool access, regulatory hold).

