### 13. Compute Type Comparison

| Aspect | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) | All-Purpose Cluster | Job Cluster |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Purpose** | SQL queries, BI dashboards, ad-hoc analytics | Interactive dev (Python, Scala, R, SQL) | Scheduled production jobs |
| **Startup time** | Seconds (Serverless) | 5-10 minutes | 5-10 minutes |
| **Auto-scaling** | Yes (instant) | Yes (slower) | Yes |
| **Auto-stop** | Yes (configurable) | Yes (configurable) | Terminates after job completes |
| **Photon** | Always enabled | Optional | Optional |
| **Languages** | SQL only | Python, SQL, Scala, R | Python, SQL, Scala, R |
| **Cost** | Pay per query (DBU/hour while running) | DBU/hour while cluster is up | DBU/hour while job runs |
| **Cost efficiency** | Best for sporadic SQL | Most expensive (sits idle) | Best for scheduled workloads |
| **Concurrency** | High (multi-user) | Limited (shared cluster) | Single job |
| **Best for** | SQL analytics, INSERT queries | Notebook development with Python/ML | Nightly ETL pipelines, scheduled jobs |
| **Unity Catalog** | Full support | Full support | Full support |

**When to use which:**

| Scenario | Best Choice |
| --- | --- |
| Ad-hoc SQL exploration | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) |
| Dashboard serving for many users | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) |
| Python ML model training | All-Purpose Cluster with ML Runtime |
| Nightly ETL pipeline | Job Cluster via Lakeflow Jobs |
| One-off data investigation | SQL Warehouse |
| Streaming workload | All-Purpose or Job Cluster |

