### 14. Complete Optimization Checklist

| # | Check | Why | Impact |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Filter early — WHERE on partition column | Eliminates files before reading | HIGH |
| 2 | SELECT only needed columns | Parquet reads only requested columns | MEDIUM |
| 3 | Avoid `SELECT *` in subqueries/CTEs | Carries unnecessary columns through shuffles | MEDIUM |
| 4 | Use Delta format for all tables | Stats, caching, auto-optimize | HIGH |
| 5 | Run `ANALYZE TABLE` on large tables | Gives optimizer accurate row counts for join strategy selection | HIGH |
| 6 | Avoid non-equi joins on large tables | `BETWEEN` joins cannot use hash/sort-merge — use broadcast or pre-filter | HIGH |
| 7 | Pre-filter before JOIN | Reduce rows entering the join | HIGH |
| 8 | Check for spill to disk in query profile | Spill = memory pressure = slow | HIGH |
| 9 | Use `OPTIMIZE` + Z-ORDER or Liquid Clustering | Co-locates data for common filters | MEDIUM |
| 10 | Right-size your warehouse | Too small = spill + many waves; too big = wasted cost | MEDIUM |
| 11 | Avoid redundant self-joins | Self-joining a table with no filter returns every row unchanged | CRITICAL |
| 12 | Use `EXPLAIN EXTENDED` to inspect plan | Verify join types, scan types, predicate pushdown | DIAGNOSTIC |
| 13 | Check file sizes (`DESCRIBE DETAIL table`) | Ideal: 64-256 MB per file; too small = overhead, too big = poor parallelism | MEDIUM |
| 14 | Partition by low-cardinality date column | Enables partition pruning | HIGH |
| 15 | Avoid type casts in JOIN conditions | `INT(col_a) = INT(col_b)` prevents predicate pushdown | MEDIUM |
| 16 | Use broadcast hints for known small tables | `/*+ BROADCAST(small_table) */` | MEDIUM |
| 17 | Limit `ROW_NUMBER` scope | Window functions sort + partition all data | MEDIUM |
| 18 | Run `OPTIMIZE` after large writes | Compacts small files, improves future read performance | MEDIUM |
| 19 | Enable result caching | Repeated queries hit cache automatically | LOW-MEDIUM |
| 20 | Monitor query profile after every heavy query | Catch regressions early | ONGOING |

